// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO34 - internal power-control line (LDO2/
// RGB_PWR), not general-purpose. Independently re-verified 2026-07-14:
// the official Espressif arduino-esp32 upstream variant file
// (github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/Bee_Data_Logger/pins_arduino.h)
// declares `static const uint8_t LDO2 = 34;` / `static const uint8_t
// RGB_PWR = 34;` - a real, named internal LDO/RGB-power-enable line, not
// a general-purpose GPIO (this repo's own pins_arduino.h deliberately
// omits that declaration, matching the "not general-purpose" exclusion).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - re-confirmed 2026-07-14 via the
// same official Espressif upstream pins_arduino.h (declares
// `static const uint8_t BOOT_BTN = 0;`) plus independent CNX Software
// coverage (https://www.cnx-software.com/2023/07/07/bee-data-logger-esp32-s3-board-rtc-microsd-slot-qwiic-connectors-for-sensors/)
// which lists "Boot and Reset buttons" as a physical board feature.
// GPIO40 tagged "led_neopixel" - re-confirmed via the same upstream file
// (`static const uint8_t RGB_DATA = 40;`, `#define RGB_BUILTIN LED_BUILTIN`
// wired to rgbLedWrite()) plus independent coverage confirming an onboard
// RGB LED: Hackster.io (https://www.hackster.io/news/smart-bee-design-s-bee-data-logger-is-a-compact-low-power-board-built-atop-espressif-s-esp32-s3-59786f1bdeb6),
// CNX Software (above), and the vendor's own Arduino helper library
// (https://github.com/strid3r21/BeeDataLogger-Arduino-Helper, exposes
// setPixelColor()/setPixelPower()/setLDO2Power() functions confirming
// both the NeoPixel and the LDO2/RGB_PWR power-gate are real hardware).
